{"step_index":31,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-11-18T04:48:37Z","input_tokens":15939,"cache_read_tokens":119986,"output_tokens":5394,"thinking":"Initial inspection of the Blender scenes revealed details. Thorough examination of all aspects across both scenes is paramount.\n\n\nWorkspace files and redundant models across scenes require auditing. The project includes `.blend` and `.blend1` backups, especially in the `LATEST/` directory. Examination will determine if the clay version of `v5_stage_anim.blend` is still necessary, or where it should be moved.\n\n\nAnalysis indicates the presence of extraneous files and potential redundancies. The `_unrelated` directory contains obsolete assets. The `pipeline` directory shows active upstream input files and backups. The `archive/blend/` directory holds multiple versions of several assets.\n\nThe `v5_stage_anim.blend` and `v4_stage_anim.blend` scenes need internal examination to verify their contents.\n\n\nThe high object count and mesh vertex data in `v5_stage_anim.blend` suggests inefficiency. The presence of both Red Bull/Oracle decals and Mercedes stripes on the same car model raises a potential asset conflict or accidental import. Reviewing the decal and stripe assignments will clarify if the model has a redundant mesh.\n\n\nInvestigating the Blender scene objects is critical to understanding the vertex count discrepancy. Suspect that the `DEC_*_PATCH` objects are unnecessarily complex. The python script `v5_anim.py` contains a critical logic error. The light linking code incorrectly includes all car meshes because of an incorrect string comparison.\n\n\nThe light linking is fundamentally flawed. The incorrect string comparison in the script means the car body meshes are *not* being illuminated, only the decals. This explains the extreme vertex count disparity. The `v5_stage_anim.blend` scene exhibits disorganized collection management, with cameras and lights placed directly in the scene root instead of within dedicated collections as they should be, and empty collections from older versions.\n\n\nThe scene's performance issues stem from the excessive object count generated for seemingly simple assets like grandstands. A single logical grandstand is instantiated as hundreds of discrete, unparented objects, severely hindering editing operations. The script responsible for creating these environment objects needs careful review to optimize object generation and collection hierarchy.\n\n\nThe grandstand structure is fundamentally flawed, using tiny, un-parented cube objects instead of proper beams and unnecessarily duplicating mesh data. The script generates multiple unrelated objects for simple elements, like truss supports, which should be part of the same mesh. The `brake_board` code has an obvious logic error. The variable `d` is not being used to offset the pole mesh, so all the poles are overlapping.\n\n\nThe script's core issues involve unparented objects, leading to major positional inconsistencies. Numerous elements, such as brake poles, grandstand legs, bridge components, marshals, and even pit box lines, are created as independent objects, and not parented to any relevant parent object. This design causes issues with transformations. Multiple mesh instances are generated as separate objects where a single mesh with instancing would have been sufficient.\n\n\nThe script's face index calculation is fundamentally flawed. The `base` variable, intended to offset vertex indices, is computed but never applied, resulting in overlapping faces on the first mast and missing faces on subsequent masts, leaving only floating lamp heads. This explains the observed inability to modify individual masts. This error manifests as the \"uneditable object soup\" described in the documentation.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"read_file","args":{"Path":"d:\\项目session\\blender-supercar\\pipeline\\render_v5.py"}},{"name":"read_file","args":{"Path":"d:\\项目session\\blender-supercar\\pipeline\\render_clay.py"}},{"name":"read_file","args":{"Path":"d:\\项目session\\blender-supercar\\pipeline\\v5_preview.py"}},{"name":"read_file","args":{"Path":"d:\\项目session\\blender-supercar\\pipeline\\v5_stills.py"}},{"name":"run_command","args":{"CommandLine":"$b = \"D:\\APPs\\steam\\steamapps\\common\\Blender\\blender.exe\"\n$py = @'\nimport bpy, os\nfrom mathutils import Vector\n\np = r\"D:\\项目session\\blender-supercar\\LATEST\\v5_stage_anim.blend\"\nbpy.ops.wm.open_mainfile(filepath=p)\ndeps = bpy.context.evaluated_depsgraph_get()\n\ntotal_base_verts = 0\ntotal_eval_verts = 0\nheavy_eval = []\ndegenerate = []\nby_loc = {}\n\nfor ob in bpy.data.objects:\n    if ob.type == 'MESH' and ob.data:\n        bv = len(ob.data.vertices)\n        bf = len(ob.data.polygons)\n        total_base_verts += bv\n        eob = ob.evaluated_get(deps)\n        eme = eob.to_mesh()\n        ev = len(eme.vertices)\n        ef = len(eme.polygons)\n        eob.to_mesh_clear()\n        total_eval_verts += ev\n        if ev >= 2000:\n            heavy_eval.append((ev, ef, bv, bf, ob.name, [m.type for m in ob.modifiers]))\n        if bf == 0 or bv == 0:\n            degenerate.append((ob.name, bv, bf))\n        # check loose verts\n        used_v = set()\n        for poly in ob.data.polygons:\n            used_v.update(poly.vertices)\n        loose = bv - len(used_v)\n        if loose > 0:\n            degenerate.append((ob.name + f\" (loose_verts={loose})\", bv, bf))\n        # check exact duplicate world bbox centers\n        bb = [ob.matrix_world @ Vector(c) for c in ob.bound_box]\n        center = tuple(round(sum(v[i] for v in bb)/8.0, 3) for i in range(3))\n        dims = tuple(round(max(v[i] for v in bb) - min(v[i] for v in bb), 3) for i in range(3))\n        key = (center, dims)\n        by_loc.setdefault(key, []).append(ob.name)\n\nprint(f\"Total base verts: {total_base_verts:,} | Total evaluated verts: {total_eval_verts:,}\")\nprint(\"\\nTop heavy evaluated meshes (>=2000 verts):\")\nfor ev, ef, bv, bf, nm, mods in sorted(heavy_eval, reverse=True):\n    print(f\"  {nm:38s} base={bv:6d}v/{bf:5d}f -> eval={ev:7d}v/{ef:6d}f  mods={mods}\")\n\nprint(\"\\nDegenerate / loose-vert meshes:\")\nfor item in degenerate:\n    print(\" \", item)\n\nprint(\"\\nExact overlapping bbox (center + dims) groups:\")\nfor k, names in by_loc.items():\n    if len(names) > 1:\n        print(f\"  loc={k[0]} dims={k[1]} -> {names}\")\n\nprint(\"\\nRig bones & custom props:\")\nrig = bpy.data.objects.get(\"RIG_F1_Race\")\nif rig:\n    print(\"  Bones:\", [b.name for b in rig.data.bones])\n    print(\"  Custom props:\", {k: rig[k] for k in rig.keys() if not k.startswith(\"_\")})\n    if rig.animation_data and rig.animation_data.drivers:\n        print(\"  Rig drivers:\", len(rig.animation_data.drivers))\n\n# Check drivers across all objects and materials\ndrv_count = 0\nfor datablock_coll_name in (\"objects\", \"meshes\", \"materials\", \"lights\", \"cameras\", \"armatures\"):\n    for db in getattr(bpy.data, datablock_coll_name):\n        ad = getattr(db, \"animation_data\", None)\n        if ad and ad.drivers:\n            drv_count += len(ad.drivers)\nprint(\"Total drivers in file:\", drv_count)\n\n# Check materials and images\nunused_mats = [m.name for m in bpy.data.materials if m.users == 0]\nprint(\"Unused materials:\", unused_mats)\nprint(\"Images:\")\nfor img in bpy.data.images:\n    print(f\"  {img.name:30s} users={img.users} filepath={img.filepath} exists={os.path.exists(bpy.path.abspath(img.filepath)) if img.filepath else 'N/A'}\")\n\n# Check DEC_ and GEO_MERC materials/visibility\nprint(\"\\nCar livery objects (DEC_* and GEO_MERC_*):\")\nfor ob in sorted(bpy.data.objects, key=lambda x: x.name):\n    if ob.name.startswith((\"DEC_\", \"GEO_MERC_\")):\n        mats = [m.name if m else None for m in ob.data.materials]\n        print(f\"  {ob.name:34s} verts={len(ob.data.vertices):6d} mats={mats}\")\n'@\n$tmp = \"C:\\Users\\86052\\.gemini\\antigravity\\brain\\16b5f3cb-4bce-43d1-a09a-ebf98bd665b7\\scratch\\audit_scene.py\"\nSet-Content -Path $tmp -Value $py -Encoding UTF8\n& $b -b --factory-startup -P $tmp","WaitMsBeforeAsync":10000,"toolSummary":"Deep audit of meshes, overlaps, and materials in v5_stage_anim.blend"}}]}
